{"name":"Elventree","status":"ok","title":"Elventree","pageId":33995,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Elventree\" title=\"Category:Maps of Elventree\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Elventree</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Settlement</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Cormanthor\" title=\"Cormanthor\">Cormanthor</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Moonsea\" title=\"Moonsea\">Moonsea</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p23_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p23-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Elf\" title=\"Elf\">Elves</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Half-elves\" title=\"Half-elves\">half-elves</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">humans</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p11_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p11-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"religion\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Religions</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mielikki\" title=\"Mielikki\">Mielikki</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Mystra\" title=\"Mystra\">Mystra</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Chauntea\" title=\"Chauntea\">Chauntea</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Silvanus\" title=\"Silvanus\">Silvanus</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Eldath\" title=\"Eldath\">Eldath</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Corellon_Larethian\" title=\"Corellon Larethian\">Corellon Larethian</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Rillifane_Rallathil\" title=\"Rillifane Rallathil\">Rillifane Rallathil</a>,<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p24-25_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p24-25-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Eilistraee\" title=\"Eilistraee\">Eilistraee</a><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Commerce</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"imports\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Imports</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Swords, armor, parchment, wine, seafood<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"exports\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Exports</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Fine bows and arrows, wood carvings, tapestries, <a href=\"/wiki/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">herbs</a>, medicinal plants, exotic fruit<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">History</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population1\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">900 <sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p11_2-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p11-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> (including 200 elves)<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Elventree\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Elventree\">Inhabitants of  Elventree</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Locations_in_Elventree\" title=\"Category:Locations in Elventree\">Locations in  Elventree</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a class=\"newcategory\" href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Elventree\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Elventree\">Organizations in  Elventree</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Items_from_Elventree\" title=\"Category:Items from Elventree\">Items from  Elventree</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Elventree</b> was a sylvan community in the West Branch of the <a href=\"/wiki/Moonsea\" title=\"Moonsea\">Moonsea</a> in the forest of <a href=\"/wiki/Cormanthor\" title=\"Cormanthor\">Cormanthor</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p23_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p23-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Structure\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Structure</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Government\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Government</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Trade\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trade</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Notable_Locations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notable Locations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Inhabitants\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inhabitants</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Individuals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Individuals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Appearances\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appearances</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3\"><a href=\"#Novels_&amp;_Short_Stories\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Novels &amp; Short Stories</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Games\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Games</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It was surrounded on three sides by low hills dotted with caves.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HotM-p7_7-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HotM-p7-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Structure\">Structure</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Structure\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Structure\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Elventree had been built up with wood on ruins of stone buildings. There was an elegant but natural-looking palace. There were also a number of structures in the branches of trees, which were linked by <a href=\"/wiki/Rope_ladder\" title=\"Rope ladder\">rope ladders</a>, walkways, and bridges of silver rope and white planks.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HotM-p7_7-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HotM-p7-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p254-255_8-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p254-255-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The ground was reserved for cooking fires and gathering spaces where residents met to pass news or share a song.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HotM-p7_7-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HotM-p7-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Government\">Government</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Government\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Government\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n\n<p>Elventree had no formal leadership and no formal laws, but nevertheless the inhabitants were able to live in harmony with each other and with the land.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p23_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p23-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The local <a href=\"/wiki/Heralds_of_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Heralds of Faerûn\">Herald</a> office was known as Moonsilver. <a href=\"/wiki/Elanil_Elassidil\" title=\"Elanil Elassidil\">Elanil Elassidil</a> held this position in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p26_9-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p26-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The heraldic symbol of the moon elves that populated Elventree was a black oval with the long axis oriented from lower left to upper right, a silver crescent moon drifting downward, trailing silver stars from each of its points.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-D267-81_10-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-D267-81-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>, the half-elf <a href=\"/wiki/Dessaer\" title=\"Dessaer\">Dessaer</a> was called the Lord of Elventree.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p217,221_11-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p217,221-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trade\">Trade</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Trade\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Trade\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Elventree was home to a number of fine bowyers and fletchers, as well as wood carvers. Elventree also produced <a href=\"/wiki/Herb\" title=\"Herb\">herbs</a>, medicinal plants, exotic fruit, and tapestries. It imported swords, armor, parchment, wine, and seafood.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Elventree was not on a caravan route and there were no trading houses. Supplies were brought to the town and carried away by trading parties. When the rare caravan did stop in town, it was considered a festival and the community came together to buy directly from the merchant.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-4\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Elventree was established in <a href=\"/wiki/702_DR\" title=\"702 DR\">702 DR</a>. It became a haven for <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Half-elves\" title=\"Half-elves\">half-elves</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ranger\" title=\"Ranger\">rangers</a>, artists, <a href=\"/wiki/Druid\" title=\"Druid\">druids</a>, and later an outpost for the <a href=\"/wiki/Harpers\" title=\"Harpers\">Harpers</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p23_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p23-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Locations\">Notable Locations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Notable Locations\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dt>Temples and Shrines</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Halls_of_the_Unicorn\" title=\"Halls of the Unicorn\">Halls of the Unicorn</a>: Elventree's largest temple, located in hollowed-out trunks of fallen trees and dedicated to <a href=\"/wiki/Mielikki\" title=\"Mielikki\">Mielikki</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p24-25_4-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p24-25-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Cairn_of_Mysteries\" title=\"Cairn of Mysteries\">Cairn of Mysteries</a>: A great cairn and temple dedicated to <a href=\"/wiki/Mystra\" title=\"Mystra\">Mystra</a>. It was tended to by a masked wizard known only as \"<a href=\"/wiki/The_Sentinel_(Elventree)\" title=\"The Sentinel (Elventree)\">the Sentinel</a>.\"<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p24-25_4-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p24-25-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SoH-p3_12-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SoH-p3-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Other shrines to <a href=\"/wiki/Chauntea\" title=\"Chauntea\">Chauntea</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Silvanus\" title=\"Silvanus\">Silvanus</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Eldath\" title=\"Eldath\">Eldath</a>, <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Corellon_Larethian\" title=\"Corellon Larethian\">Corellon Larethian</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Rillifane_Rallathil\" title=\"Rillifane Rallathil\">Rillifane Rallathil</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p24-25_4-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p24-25-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Other Establishments</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Gold_Cave\" title=\"Gold Cave\">The Gold Cave</a>: One of the few shops in Elventree, this cave provided all the basics for travel but little else. It was run by the half-elf <a href=\"/wiki/Amaril_Sweetwater\" title=\"Amaril Sweetwater\">Amaril Sweetwater</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-5\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU3dheWluZ19Cb3VnaD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Swaying Bough (page does not exist)\">The Swaying Bough</span>: An inn located in the branches of a giant oak tree. The proprietor in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/Emric\" title=\"Emric\">Emric</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVHJlZV9TcGlyaXRzP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Tree Spirits (page does not exist)\">The Tree Spirits</span>: A fine tavern.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p11_2-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p11-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Other</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Listening_Tree\" title=\"Listening Tree\">Listening Tree</a>: A giant <a href=\"/wiki/Oak\" title=\"Oak\">oak</a> standing in the center of Elventree. The branches of the tree itself served as an amphitheater; performances happened here regularly.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Environs</dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_the_Harp_(Elventree)\" title=\"House of the Harp (Elventree)\">House of the Harp</a>: A stone harp outside a fieldstone hut in a ravine just outside of town marked a base for the Harpers. The hut led into an underground headquarters with cave rooms and tunnels that linked to other caves in Elventree. The House of the Harp was operated by <a href=\"/wiki/Shalaer\" title=\"Shalaer\">Shalaer</a>, the ghost of a half-elven <a href=\"/wiki/Bard\" title=\"Bard\">bard</a> who communicated with the half-dozen Harpers living in the area. Wands of <i><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTGlnaHRuaW5nP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Lightning (page does not exist)\">lightning</span></i> and <i><a href=\"/wiki/Magic_missile\" title=\"Magic missile\">magic missile</a></i> were set up to protect the base.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p26_9-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p26-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRGFuY2luZ19TdG9uZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Dancing Stone (page does not exist)\">The Dancing Stone</span>: A site sacred to the worshipers of Eilistraee was located in the vicinity. Because of that, a number of Eilistraeeans (both drow and otherwise) were welcome in the town.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p255_13-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p255-13\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inhabitants\">Inhabitants</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Inhabitants\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Elventree was a modest community largely comprising nonhuman refugees from <a href=\"/wiki/Hillsfar\" title=\"Hillsfar\">Hillsfar</a>'s Great Law of Humanity.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HotM-p7_7-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HotM-p7-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Its population of 900 included 200 elves, mostly <a href=\"/wiki/Wood_elf\" title=\"Wood elf\">wood elves</a>, who were viewed as representatives of the <a href=\"/wiki/Elven_Court\" title=\"Elven Court\">Elven Court</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p25_6-8\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p25-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Individuals\">Individuals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Individuals\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Individuals\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Elanil_Elassidil\" title=\"Elanil Elassidil\">Elanil Elassidil</a>, Herald in <a href=\"/wiki/1367_DR\" title=\"1367 DR\">1367 DR</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-M-p26_9-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-M-p26-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Dessaer\" title=\"Dessaer\">Dessaer</a>, Lord of Elventree (<a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>).<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p217,221_11-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p217,221-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Fandar\" title=\"Fandar\">Fandar</a>, elven swordsman (1372 DR).<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p207_14-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p207-14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Curnil\" title=\"Curnil\">Curnil</a>, black-bearded human captain (1372 DR).<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p217-218_15-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p217-218-15\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Seyll_Auzkovyn\" title=\"Seyll Auzkovyn\">Seyll Auzkovyn</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Drow\" title=\"Drow\">drow</a> high priestess of <a href=\"/wiki/Eilistraee\" title=\"Eilistraee\">Eilistraee</a> and advisor to Lord Dessaer. (Seyll likely did not reside in Elventree itself, but rather in the vicinity with other Eilistraeeans.)<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Condemn-p221_16-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Condemn-p221-16\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>16<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appearances\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Appearances\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"block-indent\"><h4><span id=\"Novels_.26_Short_Stories\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Novels_&amp;_Short_Stories\">Novels &amp; Short Stories</span></h4><div class=\"block-indent\"><i><a href=\"/wiki/Condemnation\" title=\"Condemnation\">Condemnation</a></i></div><h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Games\">Video Games</span></h4><div class=\"block-indent\"><i><a href=\"/wiki/Neverwinter_Nights:_Tyrants_of_the_Moonsea\" title=\"Neverwinter Nights: Tyrants of the Moonsea\">Neverwinter Nights: Tyrants of the Moonsea</a></i></div></div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Elventree?veaction=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-M-p23-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p23_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p23_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p23_1-2\">1.2</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p23_1-3\">1.3</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/John_Terra\" title=\"John Terra\">John Terra</a> (January 1995). “Reference Guide”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Allison_Lassieur\" title=\"Allison Lassieur\">Allison Lassieur</a> ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Moonsea_(accessory)\" title=\"The Moonsea (accessory)\">The Moonsea</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 23. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0786900923\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0786900923\">978-0786900923</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-M-p11-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p11_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-M-p11_2-1\">